{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The expression for $g(x)$ includes $\\cos(x)$.\n\nRemember that the derivative of $\\cos(x)$ is $-\\sin(x)$.\n\nPut another way, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\cos(x)]=-\\sin(x)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[-8x-\\cos(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x)-\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\cos(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\cdot (1)-(-\\sin(x))\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8+\\sin(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$g'(x)=-8+\\sin(x)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $g(x)=-8x-\\cos(x)$.\n\n$g'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"-8+\\sin\\left(x\\right)"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
